{#
calendar/_subscribe.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Which of a connection's calendars to mirror.

A hand-written form rather than a Symfony one, because there is no entity behind
it: the submission is a set of opaque remote ids, and every property of every
calendar is re-read from the remote on the way through
(CalendarSubscriber). A form type mapping name, colour and read-only would be a
form type whose fields must be ignored, which is worse than not having them.

Two states, one markup block. When discovery failed there is no list and the
reason takes its place — a Google account whose consent screen had the calendar
scope unticked answers here, with a sentence naming the fix. That is the whole
reason this screen catches the exception rather than letting it 500: the person
reading it is already asking "why are there no calendars?".

Wrapped in the modal frame directly rather than through _modal_form.html.twig,
which needs a FormView it does not have. The frame is what Turbo swaps into; a
response without it leaves the dialog on its spinner.

Variables:
  subscriptions  CalendarSubscription[]  every calendar the source offers
  sourceKind     string                  'account' | 'integration'
  sourceId       int                     the account's or connection's id
  sourceLabel    string                  what to call it on screen
  error          string|null             why there is no list
#}
{% extends '_layout/app.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
<turbo-frame id="modal">
    <template data-ui--modal-frame-title>{{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.title'|trans }}</template>

    <form method="post"
          action="{{ path('app_settings_calendar_subscribe', { kind: sourceKind, id: sourceId }) }}"
          data-turbo-frame="modal"
          class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar-subscribe' ~ sourceKind ~ sourceId) }}">

        <div class="flex-1 min-h-0 px-6 pb-6 space-y-5 overflow-y-auto">
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                {{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.intro'|trans({ '%name%': sourceLabel }) }}
            </p>

            {% if error is not null %}
                <div role="alert" class="flex items-start gap-2.5 rounded-lg alert-danger px-3.5 py-3 text-sm text-danger">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <p class="leading-snug">{{ error }}</p>
                </div>

            {% elseif subscriptions is empty %}
                <p class="py-6 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
                    {{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.empty'|trans({ '%name%': sourceLabel }) }}
                </p>

            {% else %}
                <ul class="divide-y divide-line">
                    {% for subscription in subscriptions %}
                        {% set remote = subscription.remote %}
                        {% set local  = subscription.local %}
                        {# The default calendar is where a new event lands, so
                           unticking it would make the next thing the user
                           creates vanish on save — the same rule that hides
                           the delete button on it in the settings list.
                           CalendarSubscriber refuses it server-side too; this
                           is the half a person meets. #}
                        {% set locked = local is not null and local.isDefault %}
                        {% set field  = 'remote-calendar-' ~ loop.index %}

                        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 py-2.5">
                            <input type="checkbox"
                                   id="{{ field }}"
                                   name="remoteIds[]"
                                   value="{{ remote.remoteId }}"
                                   {% if subscription.isSubscribed %}checked{% endif %}
                                   {% if locked %}disabled{% endif %}
                                   class="mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 rounded border-field text-accent focus:ring-accent cursor-pointer">

                            {# The disabled box submits nothing, so the ticked
                               state has to travel some other way or saving
                               would unsubscribe the default calendar the box
                               was disabled to protect. #}
                            {% if locked %}
                                <input type="hidden" name="remoteIds[]" value="{{ remote.remoteId }}">
                            {% endif %}

                            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 mt-1.5 rounded-full shrink-0"
                                  style="background-color: {{ local ? local.color : (remote.color ?: '#71717a') }}"
                                  aria-hidden="true"></span>

                            <label for="{{ field }}" class="flex-1 min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-0.5 cursor-pointer">
                                <span class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
                                    <span class="truncate text-sm text-ink">{{ remote.name }}</span>

                                    {% if remote.isPrimary %}
                                        <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium bg-accent/10 text-accent">
                                            {{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.primary'|trans }}
                                        </span>
                                    {% endif %}

                                    {% if remote.isReadOnly %}
                                        <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium bg-zinc-500/10 text-ink-muted"
                                              title="{{ 'settings.calendars.read_only_hint'|trans }}">
                                            <i class="fa-solid fa-lock mr-1 text-[8px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                            {{ 'settings.calendars.read_only'|trans }}
                                        </span>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </span>

                                {% if locked %}
                                    <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                                        {{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.default_locked'|trans }}
                                    </span>
                                {% elseif subscription.isSubscribed %}
                                    <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                                        {{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.mirrored'|trans }}
                                    </span>
                                {% endif %}
                            </label>
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>

                {# Said before the button rather than in a confirmation after
                   it: unticking deletes a calendar, and the one thing a person
                   needs to know is that what only exists here is moved rather
                   than deleted with it. #}
                <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.unsubscribe_note'|trans }}
                </p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2 px-6 pb-6 pt-3 shrink-0">
            <button type="button"
                    data-action="click->ui--modal#close"
                    class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-8 px-3.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                           text-ink-soft bg-field border border-field hover:bg-hover
                           focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                           transition-colors duration-100">{{ 'form.cancel'|trans }}</button>

            {% if error is null %}
                <button type="submit"
                        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-8 px-3.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium text-white
                               bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong active:bg-blue-800
                               focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                               transition-colors duration-100">{{ 'settings.calendars.subscribe.save'|trans }}</button>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </form>
</turbo-frame>
{% endblock %}
